WEBVTT

00:00:57.918 --> 00:01:02.113
And to marathons at the North Pole,
and from Everest Base Camp.

00:01:03.312 --> 00:01:07.019
When I asked him what had led
to this high-octane life,

00:01:07.043 --> 00:01:09.161
he quoted Nietzsche:

00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:13.552
"He, who has a Why to live,
can bear with almost any How."

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:18.002
He had come across the quote
in a really beautiful book

00:01:18.026 --> 00:01:21.609
called "Man's Search for Meaning,"
by Viktor Frankl,

00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:23.839
a neurologist and psychiatrist

00:01:23.863 --> 00:01:27.063
who survived years
in a Nazi concentration camp.

00:01:27.561 --> 00:01:31.792
Frankl used this Nietzsche quote
to explain to us